        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is delayed onset muscle soreness (DOMS)?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Delayed onset muscle soreness is the stiffness and tenderness that shows up 12 to 24 hours after exercise and peaks around 24 to 72 hours. It comes from minor muscle damage, the inflammation that follows, and nerve endings in the muscle becoming more sensitive. It's strongest after new exercises and after the lowering (eccentric) part of a lift. It's normal, it isn't a sign of a good or bad workout, and it fades on its own."
        }
