        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Aim for at least 1.2 grams per kilogram of bodyweight per day, and about 1.6 g/kg if you lift regularly or are losing weight. For a 180-pound man (82 kg), that's about 98 to 131 grams a day. Spread it across 3 to 4 meals of roughly 30 to 40 grams each. Your daily total matters more than exact timing: muscles stay primed for 24 hours or more after training, so a protein meal within a few hours of your workout is plenty."
        }
      },
