        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Is it normal to be sore after every workout after 50?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Some soreness after a new or harder workout is normal at any age. Being sore after every routine workout usually means your training is irregular or jumps in difficulty too quickly. Train the same movements 2 to 3 times a week and increase the load gradually, and soreness typically drops a lot within a few weeks. If you have severe pain, major swelling, or dark-colored urine after exercise, see a doctor, as those can be signs of a rare but serious condition called rhabdomyolysis."
