      <ul>
        <li>Soreness that lasts 3 days usually comes from a workout that was new, harder than usual, or heavy on lowering the weight, not from your age.</li>
        <li>A 2025 meta-analysis found older adults don't get more muscle damage or soreness than younger adults.</li>
        <li>The biggest fix is consistency: after even one session, the same workout causes far less soreness the next time (the "repeated bout effect").</li>
        <li>Protein doesn't erase soreness much, but it helps muscles keep their strength after a hard session and rebuild stronger. Aim for at least 1.2 g/kg a day (about 1.6 g/kg if you lift), in meals of 30–40g.</li>
